{
  "id": 529703817,
  "iid": 26431,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TSDNS: Guard request domain extraction against short packets",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn dissect_tsdns(), request packets are assumed to end with a 5-byte delimiter. If a packet has fewer than 5 bytes, pLen - 5 underflows into a negative integer. This causes tvb_get_string_enc() to treat the length as an unsigned 4GB value (triggering excessive memory allocation attempts) and causes proto_tree_add_item() to throw an exception.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added checks ensuring pLen is at least 5 bytes before extracting the request domain string and adding it to the tree.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-09-09T03:01:56.212Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-10T10:53:05.971Z",
