      "title": "tsdns: reject packets shorter than 5 bytes before dissecting",
      "message": "tsdns: reject packets shorter than 5 bytes before dissecting\n\nIn TSDNS, queries end with a 5-byte delimiter (\\n\\r\\r\\r\\n) and responses contain IP:port pairs. When a packet has fewer than 5 bytes, extracting the query string with pLen - 5 causes a negative length exception in tvb_get_string_enc().\n\nCheck tvb_reported_length(tvb) < 5 at the beginning of dissect_tsdns() and return 0 immediately. This avoids touching protocol columns or allocating memory for invalid/truncated packets.",
      "author_name": "meel-ayush",
      "author_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-09-10T10:11:27.000+00:00",
      "committer_name": "meel-ayush",
