      "title": "TSDNS: Guard request domain extraction against short packets",
      "message": "TSDNS: Guard request domain extraction against short packets\n\nIn dissect_tsdns(), request packets are assumed to have a 5-byte trailer (\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n). If a request packet contains fewer than 5 bytes, pLen - 5 evaluates to a negative value. When passed to tvb_get_string_enc() (which expects an unsigned length), this leads to integer underflow, excessive memory allocation attempts, and dissector errors.\n\nEnsure pLen is at least 5 bytes before extracting the domain string.",
      "author_name": "meel-ayush",
      "author_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-09-09T03:01:27.000+00:00",
      "committer_name": "meel-ayush",
      "committer_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
